    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.test\n\n### Question\n\n1. How do I disable ANSI colors in the output? Neovim ex-command output doesn't handle them.\r\n2. An `'errorformat'` that can read the error report from `mini.test`.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.test</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>How do I disable ANSI colors in the output? Neovim ex-command output doesn't handle them.</li>\n<li>An <code class=\"notranslate\">'errorformat'</code> that can read the error report from <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.test</code>.</li>\n</ol>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.test\nQuestion\n\nHow do I disable ANSI colors in the output? Neovim ex-command output doesn't handle them.\nAn 'errorformat' that can read the error report from mini.test.",
